WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.380
Single mom and assistant principal,

2
00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:06.070
Denise Winchester, wrote into our show.

3
00:00:06.070 --> 00:00:08.140
And she's been sleeping in her living room

4
00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:09.520
for the past 10 years

5
00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:13.530
and has finally moved into her very own room.

6
00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:16.840
And now she needs our help redecorating the living room

7
00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:18.340
without breaking the bank.

8
00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:19.770
So here she is now.

9
00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:21.719
Hello, Denise.
Hi, Drew.

10
00:00:21.719 --> 00:00:23.919
I'm so happy you came here.

11
00:00:23.919 --> 00:00:25.260
Thank you.

12
00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:28.180
Now you have been sleeping in your living room

13
00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:30.340
for the past 10 years.

14
00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:32.763
May I ask why?
Sure.

15
00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:36.400
A little over 10 years ago,

16
00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:39.820 line:15%
my daughter and I moved into our apartment in Manhattan.

17
00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:42.973 line:15%
It's a pretty tiny apartment, as they are in Manhattan,

18
00:00:43.990 --> 00:00:45.300
but it has two bedrooms

19
00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:46.880
and it also has what I like to call

20
00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:49.770
the world's tiniest living room.

21
00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:53.030
So, obviously, I wanted my daughter to have a room.

22
00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:54.690
So she immediately, non-negotiable,

23
00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:56.340
got like the good room, you know?

24
00:00:57.670 --> 00:00:59.263
That's how we do, right?

25
00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.040
But I saw an opportunity there.

26
00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:07.040
And I said, "I'm gonna rent what would be my room,"

27
00:01:07.690 --> 00:01:10.370
and that left me in the tiny living room.

28
00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:13.000
And we're talking about a tiny box, right?

29
00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:14.930
But when you're a mom,

30
00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:16.720
especially a single mom,

31
00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:18.940
you do what you gotta do, right?

32
00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:20.530
Any parent does I think.

33
00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:24.420
So I did it, of course, to save money for bills

34
00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:25.410
and the necessities.

35
00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:27.820
But I feel like, more than that,

36
00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:32.820 line:15%
I wanted to give my daughter like an awesome childhood.

37
00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:35.020 line:15%
Like all the New York City experiences

38
00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:38.760 line:15%
that I probably wouldn't have been able to afford otherwise.

39
00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:42.443
I wanted to give her an awesome birthday party every year,

40
00:01:43.595 --> 00:01:46.350
all the holiday events, and just everything.

41
00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:47.910
I never wanted her to feel

42
00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:53.030
like she wasn't worthy of all of that, because she is,

43
00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:55.470
and I never wanted her to feel deprived.

44
00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:58.543
And that's why I did it, and I would do it again.

45
00:01:59.687 --> 00:02:01.185
Aw!

46
00:02:01.185 --> 00:02:04.185
(audience clapping)

47
00:02:06.230 --> 00:02:08.810
Well, your daughter is here with us.

48
00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:11.840
Waverly, hello.
Hi.

49
00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:13.113
Hi, cutie.

50
00:02:13.970 --> 00:02:15.420
How old are you?

51
00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:16.253
I'm 13.

52
00:02:16.253 --> 00:02:18.560
What does it mean for you

53
00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:21.640
to see your mom make these choices?

54
00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:23.360
Well, I'm really thankful.

55
00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:26.090
Like I'm thankful that I got to have my own room.

56
00:02:26.090 --> 00:02:28.440 line:15%
Like I've slept on the couch before,

57
00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:30.520 line:15%
it isn't really that comfortable.

58
00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:35.370 line:15%
And just to say that she did that for like over 10 years,

59
00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:38.060
and that really made me really grateful.

60
00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:40.490
Like she did that so I could have my room

61
00:02:40.490 --> 00:02:42.939
and that just makes me feel really grateful for her.

62
00:02:42.939 --> 00:02:45.979
(audience clapping)

63
00:02:45.979 --> 00:02:47.940
The second that I found out that she got her own room

64
00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:48.920
I was so happy.

65
00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:51.160
I made her like a sign for her room,

66
00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:54.273
like the minute that I found out she had her own room.

67
00:02:54.273 --> 00:02:55.988
[Drew And Audience] Aw!

68
00:02:55.988 --> 00:02:58.444
There it is.
[Drew And Audience] Aw!

69
00:02:58.444 --> 00:03:02.003
(audience clapping)

70
00:03:02.003 --> 00:03:05.210
So in the hopes of creating this new space

71
00:03:05.210 --> 00:03:08.830
that you so deserved and that you've worked so hard for,

72
00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:10.880
what are your hopes in redecorating?

73
00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:13.010
What are you looking for?

74
00:03:13.010 --> 00:03:16.450
Well, the room we've always had so much fun in

75
00:03:16.450 --> 00:03:18.420
and we're fun people.

76
00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:21.690
I feel like there's a space challenge.

77
00:03:21.690 --> 00:03:23.460
That's just how it is.

78
00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:25.490
It has like zero personality.

79
00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:28.830 line:15%
I feel like we have quite a bit of personality.

80
00:03:28.830 --> 00:03:31.910 line:15%
And it has no charm, no character, no personality,

81
00:03:31.910 --> 00:03:33.390 line:15%
and we're not comfortable there.

82
00:03:33.390 --> 00:03:36.110
We're like literally physically not comfortable.

83
00:03:36.110 --> 00:03:36.943
You wanna be inspired by the space.

84
00:03:36.943 --> 00:03:38.400
Yeah, it would be awesome.

85
00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:40.930
And you want it turnkey and taken care of,

86
00:03:40.930 --> 00:03:43.230
and given like the ideas,

87
00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:45.850
and just to kind of magic wand it?

88
00:03:45.850 --> 00:03:46.930
Oh, please, yeah.

89
00:03:46.930 --> 00:03:48.950
And I, obviously, don't wanna break the bank

90
00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:53.890
and any inspiration would be so appreciated.

91
00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:56.450
Okay, well, I know a human magic wand.

92
00:03:56.450 --> 00:03:59.390
He is Drew crew member and interior designer

93
00:03:59.390 --> 00:04:00.600
to so many people.

94
00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:01.780
If I listed their names,

95
00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:04.500
like you would just freak out.

96
00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:06.820
Mikel Welch, and he is gonna help us

97
00:04:06.820 --> 00:04:08.700
design this space on a budget.

98
00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:11.640
And I would love to see what he's cooking up

99
00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:14.610
